[/asy] Thus, $\theta=315^\circ-270^\circ=45^\circ$, and we have $$ \sin 315^\circ = -\sin\theta = -\sin 45^\circ = -\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}} = \boxed{-\tfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}} .$$Note that since $300^\circ$ is a little less than $1755^\circ$, we can also say that (this leads to the same result, as we'll see below): $$ \sin 1755^\circ = \sin 300^\circ=\sin (360^\circ + (-60^\circ))=\sin (-60^\circ) = -\sin (-60^\circ) = -\left({1 \over 2}\right)=\boxed{-{1 \over 2}} .$$ </think> <answer> -{1 \over 2} </answer>

